IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc-definitions`
IMPORT `ccc13-logic`

-- ccc13-trademarks.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), Part X: sections 406 to 414 (forgery of trademarks and trade descriptions).
-- Reading of the answers as in ccc13-fraud.l4. Sections 407 to 411 each state an offence and no penalty: section 412(1) states the penalty for all five,
-- so the punishment function is `s 412(1) the punishments`, which takes the offence by its section number (seam rule R1).

§ `Part X -- sections 406 to 414`

§§ `Forgery of Trademarks and Trade Descriptions -- sections 406 to 414`

-- 406 For the purposes of this Part, every one forges a trademark who (a) without the consent of the proprietor of the trademark, makes or reproduces in any manner that trademark or a mark so nearly resembling it as to be calculated to deceive; or (b) falsifies, in any manner, a genuine trademark.
-- src:7420 | Forgery of Trademarks and Trade Descriptions
-- src:7421 | Forging trademark
-- src:7422 | 406 For the purposes of this Part, every one forges a trademark who
-- src:7423 | (a) without the consent of the proprietor of the trademark, makes or reproduces in any manner that trademark or a mark so nearly resembling it as to be calculated to deceive; or
-- src:7424 | (b) falsifies, in any manner, a genuine trademark.
@ref s 406 (src:7420-7424)
GIVEN `the person acts without the consent of the proprietor of the trademark` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person makes or reproduces in any manner that trademark or a mark so nearly resembling it as to be calculated to deceive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person falsifies, in any manner, a genuine trademark` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 406 the person forges a trademark` MEANS
    IF (`the person acts without the consent of the proprietor of the trademark` AND `the person makes or reproduces in any manner that trademark or a mark so nearly resembling it as to be calculated to deceive`) OR `the person falsifies, in any manner, a genuine trademark`   -- (a), (b)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "every one forges a trademark who"

-- src:7425 | Offence
-- src:7426 | 407 Every one commits an offence who, with intent to deceive or defraud the public or any person, whether ascertained or not, forges a trademark.
@ref s 407 (src:7425-7426)
GIVEN `the person acts with intent to deceive or defraud the public or any person, whether ascertained or not` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person forges a trademark, by s 406` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 407 the conduct is the offence of forging a trademark` MEANS
    IF `the person acts with intent to deceive or defraud the public or any person, whether ascertained or not`
    THEN `the person forges a trademark, by s 406`
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one commits an offence who, with intent to deceive or defraud the public or any person, whether ascertained or not, forges a trademark"

-- 408 ... (a) passes off other wares or services as and for those ordered or required; or (b) makes use, in association with wares or services, of any description that is false in a material respect regarding (i) the kind, quality, quantity or composition, (ii) the geographical origin, or (iii) the mode of the manufacture, production or performance of those wares or services.
-- src:7427 | Passing off
-- src:7428 | 408 Every one commits an offence who, with intent to deceive or defraud the public or any person, whether ascertained or not,
-- src:7429 | (a) passes off other wares or services as and for those ordered or required; or
-- src:7430 | (b) makes use, in association with wares or services, of any description that is false in a material respect regarding
-- src:7431 | (i) the kind, quality, quantity or composition,
-- src:7432 | (ii) the geographical origin, or
-- src:7433 | (iii) the mode of the manufacture, production or performance
-- src:7434 | of those wares or services.
@ref s 408 (src:7427-7434)
GIVEN `the person acts with intent to deceive or defraud the public or any person, whether ascertained or not` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person passes off other wares or services as and for those ordered or required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person makes use, in association with wares or services, of a description that is false in a material respect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the description concerns the kind, quality, quantity or composition, the geographical origin, or the mode of the manufacture, production or performance of those wares or services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 408 the conduct is the offence of passing off` MEANS
    IF    `the person acts with intent to deceive or defraud the public or any person, whether ascertained or not`
      AND (   `the person passes off other wares or services as and for those ordered or required`   -- (a)
           OR (`the person makes use, in association with wares or services, of a description that is false in a material respect` AND `the description concerns the kind, quality, quantity or composition, the geographical origin, or the mode of the manufacture, production or performance of those wares or services`))   -- (b)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one commits an offence who, with intent to deceive or defraud the public or any person, whether ascertained or not,"

-- (2) No person shall be convicted of an offence under this section where he proves that he acted in good faith in the ordinary course of his business or employment.
-- It is a defence "where he proves": when it is not proved the answer is JUST FALSE for the defence ("this section gives no defence on these facts"), ruling of 2026-11-05 (b).
-- src:7437 | Saving
-- src:7438 | (2) No person shall be convicted of an offence under this section where he proves that he acted in good faith in the ordinary course of his business or employment.
@ref s 409(2) (src:7437-7438)
GIVEN `the person proves that they acted in good faith in the ordinary course of their business or employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 409(2) the person is saved from conviction of an offence under section 409` MEANS
    IF `the person proves that they acted in good faith in the ordinary course of their business or employment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person shall be convicted of an offence under this section where he proves that he acted in good faith in the ordinary course of his business or employment"; this section gives no defence on these facts

-- src:7435 | Instruments for forging trademark
-- src:7436 | 409 (1) Every one commits an offence who makes, has in his possession or disposes of a die, block, machine or other instrument designed or intended to be used in forging a trademark.
@ref s 409(1) (src:7435-7436)
GIVEN `the person makes, has in their possession or disposes of a die, block, machine or other instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is designed or intended to be used in forging a trademark` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defence applies, by s 409(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 409(1) the conduct is the offence of having an instrument for forging a trademark` MEANS
    IF `the person makes, has in their possession or disposes of a die, block, machine or other instrument` AND `the instrument is designed or intended to be used in forging a trademark`
    THEN `ccc13 not` `the defence applies, by s 409(2)`   -- JUST FALSE when the defence applies; NOTHING carried
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one commits an offence who makes, has in his possession or disposes of a die, block, machine or other instrument designed or intended to be used in forging a trademark"

-- 410 ... with intent to deceive or defraud, (a) defaces, conceals or removes a trademark or the name of another person from anything without the consent of that other person; or (b) being a manufacturer, dealer, trader or bottler,
-- fills any bottle or siphon that bears the trademark or name of another person, without the consent of that other person, with a beverage, milk, by-product of milk or other liquid commodity for the purpose of sale or traffic.
-- src:7439 | Other offences in relation to trademarks
-- src:7440 | 410 Every one commits an offence who, with intent to deceive or defraud,
-- src:7441 | (a) defaces, conceals or removes a trademark or the name of another person from anything without the consent of that other person; or
-- src:7442 | (b) being a manufacturer, dealer, trader or bottler, fills any bottle or siphon that bears the trademark or name of another person, without the consent of that other person, with a beverage, milk, by-product of milk or other liquid commodity for the purpose of sale or traffic.
@ref s 410 (src:7439-7442)
GIVEN `the person acts with intent to deceive or defraud` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person defaces, conceals or removes a trademark or the name of another person from anything` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a manufacturer, dealer, trader or bottler and fills a bottle or siphon that bears the trademark or name of another person with a beverage, milk, by-product of milk or other liquid commodity for the purpose of sale or traffic` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts without the consent of that other person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 410 the conduct is the offence of other offences in relation to trademarks` MEANS
    IF    `the person acts with intent to deceive or defraud`
      AND `the person acts without the consent of that other person`
      AND (   `the person defaces, conceals or removes a trademark or the name of another person from anything`   -- (a)
           OR `the person is a manufacturer, dealer, trader or bottler and fills a bottle or siphon that bears the trademark or name of another person with a beverage, milk, by-product of milk or other liquid commodity for the purpose of sale or traffic`)   -- (b)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one commits an offence who, with intent to deceive or defraud,"

-- 411 Every one commits an offence who sells, exposes or has in his possession for sale, or advertises for sale, goods that have been used, reconditioned or remade and that bear the trademark or the trade-name of another person,
-- without making full disclosure that the goods have been reconditioned, rebuilt or remade for sale and that they are not then in the condition in which they were originally made or produced.
-- src:7443 | Used goods sold without disclosure
-- src:7444 | 411 Every one commits an offence who sells, exposes or has in his possession for sale, or advertises for sale, goods that have been used, reconditioned or remade and that bear the trademark or the trade-name of another person, without making full disclosure that the goods have been reconditioned, rebuilt or remade for sale and that they are not then in the condition in which they were originally made or produced.
@ref s 411 (src:7443-7444)
GIVEN `the person sells, exposes or has in their possession for sale, or advertises for sale, the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the things are goods, by s 379` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the goods have been used, reconditioned or remade` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the goods bear the trademark or the trade-name of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person makes full disclosure that the goods have been reconditioned, rebuilt or remade for sale and that they are not then in the condition in which they were originally made or produced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 411 the conduct is the offence of selling used goods without disclosure` MEANS
    IF    `the person sells, exposes or has in their possession for sale, or advertises for sale, the goods`
      AND `the goods have been used, reconditioned or remade`
      AND `the goods bear the trademark or the trade-name of another person`
      AND NOT `the person makes full disclosure that the goods have been reconditioned, rebuilt or remade for sale and that they are not then in the condition in which they were originally made or produced`
    THEN `the things are goods, by s 379`   -- JUST TRUE when they are goods; JUST FALSE (the "means" of section 379) when not; NOTHING carried
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one commits an offence who sells, exposes or has in his possession for sale, or advertises for sale, goods that have been used, reconditioned or remade"

-- 412 (1) Every one who commits an offence under section 407, 408, 409, 410 or 411 is guilty of (a) an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years; or (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
-- src:7445 | Punishment
-- src:7446 | 412 (1) Every one who commits an offence under section 407, 408, 409, 410 or 411 is guilty of
-- src:7447 | (a) an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years; or
-- src:7448 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 412(1) (src:7445-7448)
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Punishment)
`s 412(1) the punishments` MEANS
    IF    `the offence`'s section EQUALS 407
       OR `the offence`'s section EQUALS 408
       OR `the offence`'s section EQUALS 409
       OR `the offence`'s section EQUALS 410
       OR `the offence`'s section EQUALS 411
    THEN JUST (LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- (a)
                  , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`)   -- (b) the text states no penalty: s 787(1)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence under section 407, 408, 409, 410 or 411"

@ref s 412(1) (the class of the offence) (src:7445-7448)
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Class of offence`)
`s 412(1) the class of the offence` MEANS
    IF    `the offence`'s section EQUALS 407
       OR `the offence`'s section EQUALS 408
       OR `the offence`'s section EQUALS 409
       OR `the offence`'s section EQUALS 410
       OR `the offence`'s section EQUALS 411
    THEN JUST `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence under section 407, 408, 409, 410 or 411"

-- (2) Anything by means of or in relation to which a person commits an offence under section 407, 408, 409, 410 or 411 is, unless the court otherwise orders, forfeited on the conviction of that person for that offence.
-- "unless the court otherwise orders" once met: decided case by case, fork F6: JUST FALSE, the forfeiture does not follow.
-- src:7449 | Forfeiture
-- src:7450 | (2) Anything by means of or in relation to which a person commits an offence under section 407, 408, 409, 410 or 411 is, unless the court otherwise orders, forfeited on the conviction of that person for that offence.
@ref s 412(2) (src:7449-7450)
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the thing is something by means of or in relation to which the person commits the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is convicted of that offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 412(2) the thing is forfeited` MEANS
    IF NOT (   `the offence`'s section EQUALS 407
            OR `the offence`'s section EQUALS 408
            OR `the offence`'s section EQUALS 409
            OR `the offence`'s section EQUALS 410
            OR `the offence`'s section EQUALS 411)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence under section 407, 408, 409, 410 or 411"
    ELSE IF NOT (`the thing is something by means of or in relation to which the person commits the offence` AND `the person is convicted of that offence`)
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "forfeited on the conviction of that person for that offence"
         ELSE IF `the court otherwise orders`
              THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the court otherwise orders"
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:7451 | 413 [Repealed, 2018, c. 29, s. 47]
@ref s 413 (src:7451-7451)
`s 413 as the text shows it` MEANS "413 [Repealed, 2018, c. 29, s. 47]"

-- 414 Where, in proceedings under this Part, the alleged offence relates to imported goods, evidence that the goods were shipped to Canada from a place outside Canada is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary,
-- proof that the goods were made or produced in the country from which they were shipped.
-- src:7452 | Presumption from port of shipment
-- src:7453 | 414 Where, in proceedings under this Part, the alleged offence relates to imported goods, evidence that the goods were shipped to Canada from a place outside Canada is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof that the goods were made or produced in the country from which they were shipped.
@ref s 414 (src:7452-7453)
GIVEN `the proceedings are under this Part and the alleged offence relates to imported goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence that the goods were shipped to Canada from a place outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 414 the evidence is proof that the goods were made or produced in the country from which they were shipped` MEANS
    IF NOT `the proceedings are under this Part and the alleged offence relates to imported goods`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, in proceedings under this Part, the alleged offence relates to imported goods"
    ELSE IF NOT `there is evidence that the goods were shipped to Canada from a place outside Canada`
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section makes evidence of shipment proof; where there is none it is silent
         ELSE IF `there is evidence to the contrary`
              THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of any evidence to the contrary"
              ELSE JUST TRUE
